data: {"index":1,"delta":{"text":" software engineering. While they occasionally overlap in application, they were designed with fundamentally different philosophies, target audiences, and technical constraints","type":"text"},"event_type":"step.delta"}

event: step.delta
data: {"index":1,"delta":{"text":". Python prioritizes developer velocity and simplicity; JavaScript serves as the runtime engine of the web; and Rust offers uncompromising performance","type":"text"},"event_type":"step.delta"}

event: step.delta
data: {"index":1,"delta":{"text":" and safety for systems-level tasks. Understanding how these languages compare across performance, memory management, syntax, and ecosystem is","type":"text"},"event_type":"step.delta"}

event: step.delta
data: {"index":1,"delta":{"text":" essential for modern developers.\n\n### Core Philosophy and Design Goals\n\nPython, conceived in the late 1980s","type":"text"},"event_type":"step.delta"}

